      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793531968512,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Data model\nThe data model is what makes SmartThings a platform rather than a list of integrations. Every protocol is mapped onto the same tree, and the app draws its UI from metadata attached to\nthat tree.\n\n\nOwnership and grouping\n    1. Samsung Account is mandatory. A user can own up to 10 locations.\n    2. Location: one owner plus members, a country, timezone and temperature scale. Hubs, devices, rooms, modes, scenes and automations belong to the location, not to a user.\n    3. Room: a subgroup of a location. Devices are assigned to at most one room.\n    4. Mode: a user-defined location state (Home, Away, Night) that rules can read and set.\n\nDevice anatomy\n    1. Component: a functional part of a device. Every device has main. A 3-gang switch has three components because a capability can appear only once per component. Limits: 10 components per\ndevice, 20 capabilities per component.\n    2. Capability: a versioned schema of attributes and commands, standard (implicit smartthings namespace) or custom (namespace.name). Values outside the schema are rejected.\n    3. Device profile: which components and capabilities a device has, plus metadata (vid, mnmn, ocfDeviceType).\n    4. Presentation: how the app draws it. Identified by vid + mnmn, generated from a device configuration.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Data model\nThe data model is what makes SmartThings a platform rather than a list of integrations. Every protocol is mapped onto the same tree, and the app draws its UI from metadata attached to that tree.\n\n\nOwnership and grouping\n    1. Samsung Account is mandatory. A user can own up to 10 locations.\n    2. Location: one owner plus members, a country, timezone and temperature scale. Hubs, devices, rooms, modes, scenes and automations belong to the location, not to a user.\n    3. Room: a subgroup of a location. Devices are assigned to at most one room.\n    4. Mode: a user-defined location state (Home, Away, Night) that rules can read and set.\n\nDevice anatomy\n    1. Component: a functional part of a device. Every device has main. A 3-gang switch has three components because a capability can appear only once per component. Limits: 10 components per device, 20 capabilities per component.\n    2. Capability: a versioned schema of attributes and commands, standard (implicit smartthings namespace) or custom (namespace.name). Values outside the schema are rejected.\n    3. Device profile: which components and capabilities a device has, plus metadata (vid, mnmn, ocfDeviceType).\n    4. Presentation: how the app draws it. Identified by vid + mnmn, generated from a device configuration.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
